flowchart
  accTitle: Response framing determines the meaning of EOF
  accDescr: Length-delimited and chunked responses can be incomplete at EOF; a close-delimited response can be HTTP-complete while application content remains insufficient.
subgraph L["Content-Length framing"]
    A["Declared 3 octets<br/>Received ab, then EOF"] --> B["HTTP incomplete: 2 of 3"]
  end
  subgraph T["Chunked framing"]
    C["Received chunk with ab<br/>EOF before terminator"] --> D["HTTP incomplete"]
  end
  subgraph E["Close-delimited framing"]
    F["Received ab, then EOF"] --> G["HTTP complete at EOF<br/>Application integrity still unproved"]
  end
  B ~~~ C
  D ~~~ F
  classDef bad fill:#FEF2F2,stroke:#DC2626,color:#111827;
  classDef pending fill:#FFFBEB,stroke:#D97706,color:#111827;
  class B,D bad;
  class G pending;
